#LyX 2.5 created this file. For more info see https://www.lyx.org/
# DL131 Live vs LyX GUI comparison corpus — one example of each common inset kind.
#
# Purpose: open this file in LyX GUI and in Live preview side by side.
#
# Inventory (INSET_CATALOG + important subtypes):
#   Collapsible chips: Foot (title+body), Note Note/Comment/Greyedout, Marginal,
#     Box, Float figure/table, Wrap figure, Branch, Caption (nested)
#   Charstyle Flex (inline, NOT chips): Code, Emph, Strong, Noun, URL
#   Plain-text marker chips (Live-only): ERT, Phantom/HPhantom/VPhantom,
#     Nomenclature (symbol + Argument description disclosure), Argument 1 Short Title
#   Index chip "Idx" with nested IndexMacro boxes (Subentry / See)
#   Other Arguments (post:, 2, …): Live silent (parent-consumed)
#   Content: Formula (inline+display), FormulaMacro, Graphics, Tabular,
#     listings, Preview (non-click bordered box)
#   Spacing chrome: space, Newline, VSpace/Newpage/Separator markers,
#     CommandInset line
#   Formatting: Quotes, SpecialChar, script super/sub
#   CommandInset: label, ref, nameref, citation, href, toc, bibtex,
#     bibitem, index_print, nomencl_print, include/input, FloatList
#   IPA/IPADeco: omitted here (needs linguistics module; see Modules/Linguistics.lyx)
#   External: stub path (no spreadsheet file in Synthetic/)
#   Accent/Ending: catalog-only; no current Help/Synthetic samples
#
# DL133: the trailing "Tracked whole-inset disclosure chips" section adds an
# inserted and a deleted variant of every disclosure-chip kind above, and
# "Tracked nested disclosure insets" nests chips inside tracked owners.
#
# URL stays inline. Charstyles stay inline.
